          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Portable or Home Standby: Which Generator Battery Do You Need?
          </h2>

          <p>
            The best battery for a generator is the one your generator was designed for. Generators do not run on their batteries: the battery only spins the starter motor for a few seconds, then the engine's charging circuit or a built-in charger keeps it topped up. That makes size, terminal layout and cold cranking amps far more important than brand. There are two kinds of generator that use a 12-volt starting battery, and they take very different batteries.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Electric-Start Portable Generators</h3>

          <p>
            Portable generators with a key or push-button start, from compact 4,000-watt models to big dual fuel units, use a small sealed battery. Sizes range from a 12V 9Ah sealed lead acid battery, through 12V 14Ah to 18Ah batteries in powersport footprints like the YTX14-BS, up to the group U1 battery found in riding mowers. If you are still choosing a generator, our guide to the <a href="/best-electric-start-generator/">best electric start generators</a> covers which models start reliably, and the <a href="/best-portable-generator/">best portable generator</a> guide covers the wider field.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Home Standby Generators</h3>

          <p>
            Permanently installed standby generators, from air-cooled home units to liquid-cooled models like those in our <a href="/best-26kw-generator/">best 26kW generator</a> guide, start from a car-style battery. Group 26R is one of the most common sizes on air-cooled home units, and larger liquid-cooled generators may call for a bigger group. The generator's own controller trickle charges the battery and runs a weekly exercise cycle, so the battery is always ready, as long as it is healthy.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Recoil-Start and Inverter Models</h3>

          <p>
            Many small inverter generators and budget portables start with a pull cord only and have no battery at all. Others have an optional electric start kit. Check before you buy: if your generator has no battery tray or starter, it does not need a battery. Our pillar guide to the <a href="/best-home-generator-for-power-outages/">best home generators for power outages</a> explains the trade-offs between portable, inverter and standby types.
          </p>
